  "answer_text": "A Socket BGP session can accommodate up to 1024 routes from a neighbor before performance is affected. To reduce the number of advertised routes, use BGP summary routes (they consolidate prefixes; up to 256 summary routes per peer and up to 5 communities per summary route). If suitable, advertise a default route (0/0) instead of all specific prefixes to further limit the number of routes sent to the neighbor.",
